Use separate VOLE rows for the CRT VOLE masks unless REUSE_CRT_WITNESS

The CRT VOLE masks are derived from garbling-style gate labels, whose offset is the prover's VOLE
input u on secpar_bits "label rows". The spec reuses the first witness rows, whose correction
d = u + w is public, so the offset is d + w there. That lets a verifier check a guess for those
witness bits, and with a correct guess, recover the masks. That is fine for FAEST, whose witness
starts with its secret key, but not for generic relations.

So by default, use secpar_bits separate rows after the witness. They are corrected and covered by
the VOLE check like the witness rows, but get no d. This adds (tau - 1) * secpar_bits / 8 bytes per
proof (256 for FAEST-EM-128f). OWFs whose witness starts with secpar_bits uniform secret bits may
set OWF_CONSTANTS::REUSE_CRT_WITNESS to keep the spec's layout. FAEST's own OWFs do, so their
signatures are unchanged.

TODO Propose this change to the faest-arch-opt authors.

